messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or signal starts the review — for example, does the engineer receive an automated notification, a manual assignment in a task system, or an email — and where does the specification document come from at that moment?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "What specific criteria or checklist does the engineer use to decide whether a new feature is correctly reflected in the document?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Can you walk me through the sequence of individual steps the engineer performs during the review, from opening the document to completing it?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "What are the possible outcomes at the end of the review, and what action or next step does each outcome trigger?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Which tools or systems does the engineer use during the review, and in what file format is the specification document typically stored?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "After the engineer completes the review, who receives the document or the review findings, and does any other role participate in the process before or after the engineer's review?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Review a specification document for feature coverage, consistency, and editorial errors.",
  "actors": [
    "document reviewer",
    "feature owner",
    "document author",
    "approver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "document repository",
    "change request tracker",
    "review checklist",
    "commenting tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "specification document",
    "feature change list",
    "previous document version",
    "review checklist"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "review comments",
    "change request list",
    "approval decision",
    "updated document"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect document and related change list",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Compare feature changes with document content",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check terminology and formatting consistency",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Record comments and requested revisions",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Revise document based on comments",
      "actor": "document author"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Confirm revisions with feature owner",
      "actor": "feature owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Approve final document",
      "actor": "approver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all feature changes reflected?",
      "branches": [
        "complete",
        "missing changes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are the revisions acceptable?",
      "branches": [
        "approve",
        "request another revision"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing change list",
    "conflicting terminology",
    "unclear feature owner",
    "unresolved comments"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Feature coverage can be checked by comparing change lists and document sections."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Terminology, formatting, and typo checks can be automated."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Review comments can be grouped by section, severity, and owner."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert answers vaguely and never commits to specifics.
Do not name any actor, system, artifact, threshold, condition or exception from the reference workflow.
Use hedged generalities such as "the person in charge usually checks it before it goes out".
Answer every question in this style, at most 30 words each.
